# play backup/relative -----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Backup screen proposed for slice 3,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host, each$
# change on the real plan/apply engine. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: backup/relative$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. hardn.yml says backupPath:$
# backups, as origin/main's Backup screen saves a relative path;$
# pkg/host/backup refuses it, and every change with it.$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Backup State         Enabled$
  [ ] Backup Path          backups Not absolute$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups off$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 3$
$
# Warning$
# "backups" is not an absolute path, so hardn refuses every$
# change. Set backupPath in /etc/hardn/hardn.yml by hand.$
$
  Nothing was written.$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Backup State         Enabled$
  [ ] Backup Path          backups Not absolute$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups off$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 1$
$
# Turn Backups Off #############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Backup State         Disabled$
   -  Rollback backups are still taken$
$
# Operation Failed$
# engine: the backups: backup: backupPath "backups" is not an$
# absolute directory (the default is /var/backups/hardn):$
# invalid backup settings (BACKUP_SETTINGS_INVALID)$
$
  Check the log file at /var/log/hardn.log for details$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Backup State         Enabled$
  [ ] Backup Path          backups Not absolute$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups off$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          None yet$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 0$
